	(text "Microphone (Rev A) - design notes\n\nKnowles SPH0641LM4H-1 (Rev D) PDM, bottom port: 1.6-3.6 V; modes by clock (sleep < 280 kHz, low power 351-815 kHz,\nnormal 1.0-4.8 MHz). SELECT = GND: firmware samples the mono channel on the PDM_CLK rising edge (nRF PDM EDGE).\nBypass C0G at the Vdd pin (Knowles: no class 2 dielectrics near the mic). R1001 links 3V3 for current measurement.\nPCB acoustic hole 0.8 mm (Knowles: 0.6-1.0 mm) through the front border region outside the LED field.\nRaw audio stays in RAM (privacy requirement, docs/firmware.md). Lifecycle: NRND/EOL per Knowles. Nothing measured."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 50.8 152.4 0)
		(effects
